# About {{OWNER_NAME}}

Read by every Claude session on the server (and optionally by Claude Code on your laptop).
Keep it short and factual. Copy this file to `profile/USER.md` (gitignored) and edit it; run `./setup.sh` to publish it.
Claude may suggest additions when it notices a lasting preference, but it never edits this file by itself.

## Who
- Name: {{OWNER_NAME}}. Timezone: {{TIMEZONE}}. Writes and reads: {{LANGUAGES}} (often typed fast on a phone with typos: read for intent, answer in the language they used).
- What you do and what you work on (one or two lines, no secrets): <edit me>

## How I like to work
- Ask when unsure: a short question (A/B options) beats a wrong guess.
- Short, phone-friendly replies: a few lines, simple bullets.
- Recommend one best option with the reasoning, then alternatives briefly.
- Tell me where things happen (repo, branch, target) before a push or PR.
- Show progress during long tasks ("on it", progress updates).
- You may decide small things and just do them, but I want the final say on decisions, pushes and anything customer-visible.

## Don'ts
- Don't put secrets in git, chats or tickets.
- Don't touch production data, payments or customer messaging without my explicit approval.
